###Deploying a Static Website on AWS S3 (https://elikplim-reborn.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/index_files/index.html)

​##Overview

​This project illustrates deploying a static website using Amazon Simple Storage Service, configuring the environment for public access, and resolving associated permission challenges.
​Process

​#Repository Setup: Initialized the project with an index.html file and an html folder dedicated to storing images and assets.
​
#Bucket Configuration: Created an S3 bucket to house the website files and enabled static website hosting in the properties.
​
#Permission Management: Configured Access Control Lists and applied a JSON bucket policy to ensure the content could be read publicly.
​Challenges Encountered
​
#Access Control Lists (ACLs): Initially, the required ACLs were not enabled, resulting in access errors. Activating them was essential for public visibility.
​
#JSON Bucket Policy: The JSON bucket policy had to be precisely defined to grant explicit permission for retrieving objects. Implementing the correct syntax resolved the final access issues.
__JSON__ 
{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Sid": "PublicReadOnlyAccess",
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Principal": "*",
            "Action": "s3:GetObject",
            "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::elikplim-reborn/*"
        }
    ]
}
